      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Embedding Provider**\n\nOkay, I've decided to use the `openai` library to generate text embeddings. I'll be using the `text-embedding-ada-002` model specifically. Now I'm focused on integrating this into a Python script, named `embed_text.py`.\n\n\n**Implementing Embedding Functionality**\n\nI'm now in the process of implementing the embedding functionality within `embed_text.py`. The focus is on incorporating the `openai` library to generate embeddings. The `text-embedding-ada-002` model is the chosen tool. I will ensure the code explicitly imports `openai` and identifies the specific model being used.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789866311918,
          "start": 1789866310358
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc587ad6001ic5gwoK5TFf3SN",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc5874d9001zr2r4BMZQvt2iA",
      "session_id": "ses_f43a78bafffe8cJdlR82J7mXfX",
      "time_created": 1789866310358,
      "time_updated": 1789866311919
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "FNFfoMHhHJVYO72h",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import openai\nimport os\n\ndef embed_text(text: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates an embedding vector for a given text string using OpenAI's text-embedding-ada-002 model.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Ensure you have your OpenAI API key set as an environment variable\n    # For example: os.environ[\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"] = \"YOUR_API_KEY\"\n    if \"OPENAI_API_KEY\" not in os.environ:\n        raise EnvironmentError(\"OPENAI_API_KEY environment variable not set.\")\n\n    client = openai.OpenAI()\n    \n    response = client.embeddings.create(\n        input=[text],\n        model=\"text-embedding-ada-002\"\n    )\n    return response.data[0].embedding\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    example_text = \"This is an example sentence to be embedded.\"\n    embedding = embed_text(example_text)\n    print(f\"Embedding for '{example_text}': {embedding[:10]}...\") # Print first 10 dimensions\n    print(f\"Embedding length: {len(embedding)}\")\n",
            "filePath": "embed_text.py"
          },
